<!--
  Scars for an ideoligion that does not venerate pain.

  WHY THIS DEF EXISTS AT ALL

  Vanilla models scarification completely and we would rather have used it as-is.
  But all three of its tiers carry

      <requiredMemes><li>PainIsVirtue</li></requiredMemes>

  and IdeoFoundation filters a precept out entirely when its requiredMemes are
  absent. So an ideoligion cannot take ANY vanilla scarification precept without
  also taking PainIsVirtue - which drags in its own requireOne chain of
  Pain_Idealized, Comfort_Ignored and SlabBed_Preferred.

  That chain suits the tribes on the ice and a hard dominion on the cold moons.
  It does not suit Luna. The Society's whole character is that it is comfortable;
  making it ascetic to explain a scar would be the tail wagging the dog.

  THE ALTERNATIVE WAS WORSE. Patching requiredMemes off the vanilla precepts would
  have worked, and would also have silently handed scarification to every other
  ideoligion in anyone's game. A precept of our own is scoped to us and changes
  nothing for anybody else.

  Everything except the meme gate is vanilla's: the Scarification issue, the
  ThoughtDefs, the GotScarified event and the ScarificationCeremony ritual. The
  only new things here are the def name, the flavour, and the absent requirement.

  Structure mirrored from Ideology/Defs/PreceptDefs/Precepts_Scarification.xml.
-->
<Defs>

  <PreceptDef>
    <defName>RR_Scarification_Peerless</defName>
    <issue>Scarification</issue>
    <impact>Medium</impact>
    <displayOrderInIssue>25</displayOrderInIssue>
    <displayOrderInImpact>100</displayOrderInImpact>
    <label>the mark</label>
    <description>A scar is not damage. It is a record, cut on purpose and in one place, that says a thing was survived and by whom. A face without one is a face with nothing written on it yet.\n\nThe cut is made once, and it is made where everybody can read it.</description>
    <!--
      One scar, and only one. The reference mark is a single line from ear to jaw,
      and its meaning depends entirely on being singular - a face covered in them
      would say something else. Vanilla's Heavy and Extreme tiers cover that other
      reading and are still used by the tribes, who mean it.
    -->
    <requiredScars>1</requiredScars>
    <associatedMemes>
      <li>RR_ColorHierarchy</li>
      <li>RR_GoldWorship</li>
    </associatedMemes>
    <!--
      Deliberately NO requiredMemes. That absence is the entire reason this def is
      here; adding one would recreate the problem it was written to avoid.

      The thoughts, the event and the ritual are all vanilla's, reused rather than
      cloned so the ceremony, the mood effects and the opinion offsets behave
      exactly as a player already expects.
    -->
    <comps>
      <li Class="PreceptComp_SituationalThought">
        <thought>Scarification_Minor</thought>
        <thoughtStageDescriptions>
          <li>Scarification (1 scar required)</li>
        </thoughtStageDescriptions>
      </li>
      <li Class="PreceptComp_SituationalThought">
        <thought>Scarification_Minor_Opinion</thought>
        <thoughtStageDescriptions>
          <li>Scarification (1 scar required)</li>
        </thoughtStageDescriptions>
      </li>
      <li Class="PreceptComp_SelfTookMemoryThought">
        <eventDef>GotScarified</eventDef>
        <thought>ScarificationCeremony_Self_Minor</thought>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </PreceptDef>

</Defs>
